WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:01.560
My background was quite challenging.

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:05.000
I grew up on a council estate,
single parent family.

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:07.120
I was born
with a physical disability.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:08.960
Regardless of your background,

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:12.200
if you really want to achieve
something, you can.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:29.680
So my first tip would be...

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:33.600
So the challenge that I would have
when I was playing,

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:35.520
was that I'd make a mistake quite
early on

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:39.640
and then I'd spend effectively 60
minutes worrying about

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:43.400
what I'd done in the first 10
or 20 minutes of the game.

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:45.200
I would dwell quite a lot,

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:46.320
and it would affect me

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.840
to the point where
at half time I'd get subbed off.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:50.680
And that's the worst thing.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:53.920
But when you make a mistake, just
think forward, look forward,

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.320
think about what
you're going to do next

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:57.760
and that will take you away from the
previous error.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:00.240
So my next tip would be...

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:05.600
When I was born I was born with a
physical disability called clubfoot

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:07.880
so it's basically
where one or both your feet

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:09.400
are completely turned all the way in.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:10.680
So it got corrected

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:15.160
but my foot still has a sort
of slight angle in when I run.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:18.880
Over my career I think I've had
many times when I've had a bit of...

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:21.760
I guess, self-doubt,
very negative thoughts,

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:24.440
I really needed to work
really hard on that mental side.

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:26.040
So I came up with my mantra - 

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:28.000
I'm fit, I'm fast,
I'm athletically strong -

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:30.400
so it was all about me being
confident in my body.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:32.080
Before I played in a big game 

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:35.880
I would say to myself that mantra -
right that's me, I'm going to do it,

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:37.800
I'm going to show
people how good I am.

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:40.920
So my next tip would be to...

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:45.520
By that, I mean it's important
that people set goals

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:48.520
and when you write it down
it really does focus your mind

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:50.120
and focuses your behaviour.

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:52.960
And I think what's good
about having a structured diary

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:55.840
is that it allows you
to be organised,

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.080
it allows you to feel good about
yourself when you've done it,

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:00.600
monitoring your progress
allows you to improve.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:03.920
So my final tip would be...

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:08.320
I think it's important to recognise,
prior to a game,

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:11.000
or prior to any big event,
that you're going to deliver,

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:13.560
giving yourself time to think about
what you're about to do.

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:17.720
Early in my career, I wouldn’t
give myself that time and space

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:20.480
and I'd just go into a game
almost like a headless chicken

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:22.120
because I'd be so excited, 

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:24.000
and then as a result of that
in the first 10 minutes

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:25.200
I'd give away a penalty.

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:28.400
So I'd always say to people,
where possible, switch off.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:32.480
Prior to a big game I like to take my
dogs for a walk, I've got two dogs,

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:35.120
and that allows me to feel
quite comfortable and confident,

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:38.880
so when I have to perform,
I'm ready to go and I'm not anxious.

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:43.080
It was incredibly special to actually
achieve and win that World Cup.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:47.360
Felt happy, felt ecstatic,
felt all of those great emotions,

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:49.800
but actually the biggest emotion
that came through was relief.

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:54.760
Because we spent 12 years
building up to that point,

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:57.120
We'd lost two
World Cup finals prior to that.

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:59.400
If I'd won the World Cup
straight away with my team

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.080
it wouldn't have been that special.

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:03.080
It wouldn't have meant anything
if we haven't had that journey.

